Description
===========

This is the P600FW project, a CPU/firmware remake for the SCI Prophet 600 (http://www.vintagesynth.com/sci/p600.php).
It uses a slightly modified Teensy++ board (http://www.pjrc.com/store/teensypp_pins.html) that plugs into the Z80 socket.

Installation and usage
======================

See documentation...

History
=======
- all revisions based on Gligli V2.1 RC3
- V2.20 JS - added noise mod and new LFO waveforms step8, seq, RevSaw
- V2.21 JS - added new LFO waveforms step4
- V2.22 JS - added 4bit Triangle and 6bit Sine
- V2.23 JS - fixed patch compatibility bug introduced in V 2.22
- V2.24 JS - reverted polymod bug to RC1 behavior 
- V2.25 JS - added new vibrato waveforms and Vibrato targets
- V2.26B JS - fixed post “Tune” volume bug introduced in V2.25
- V2.28 JS - added polymod VCO A, VCO B, VCO A-B targets
- V2.29 JS - fixed error with CC 57 and 74 (LFO Shape and Vibe Shape) where not all shapes were selectable, sped up UI to V2.26B speed, Added CC 77 (Poly Mod Filter Env to modulate VCO A, VCO B, or VCO AB)
- V2.31 JS - added filter resonance as a vibrato target and increased range on the noise (or CV in for an unmodified P600) target for the vibrato
- V2.32 JS - tried to speed up volume knob
- V2.33 JS - Polymod env target PWM VCOA and VCOB, fixed bug introduced in V2.32 causing volume to drop over time
- V2.34 JS - JAM revised Arp to remove double notes and added new random mode (Thanks!!) The new random mode prevent notes to play several times in a row; each note is always different than the previous one (except if only one note is played, obviously).
- V2.5 JS - "Matrix edition". Moved to Imogen's firmware (through the Flat-Labs Z80P600 fork) and carried all V2.34 features over to it. New: arp Euclidean rhythms, step probability, swing, triplets and 32nds, ratchets; ensemble vibrato; vibrato can use all 12 LFO shapes; 8 vibrato targets; poly-mod env to PW A, PW B or both; faster panel scanning; V2.34 patches load and are converted


V2.25 includes -
LFO has 6 new waveforms:
Step8, RevSaw, Seq, Step4, Bit_Tri, Bit_Sine
New Pitch Bender targets:PW(VCO A), and VCO B only 

New noise source setting control. Pressing "to tape" 0 a second time lets you adjust the VCF CV input level and store it with a patch. I modified my P600 to add a noise source and use this parameter to adjust the noise source per patch, hence in the UI this displays as "noise". However, in an unmodified Prophet 600, this parameter controls the VCF CV input level.

Vibrato now has: 1) all LFO waveforms (CC74), 2) high and low range (CC75), and 3) target AB, A, B, VCA, Noise level, and Resonance (CC76)

Added channel aftertouch (e.g., channel pressure). If you use an external controller that has aftertouch controlling the Prophet 600, the Prophet 600 now uses this MIDI channel aftertouch data to modulate whatever the Mod-wheel is modulating. For example, I used it to apply vibrato to notes.

Added Poly-Aftertouch (e.g., per note)

Also added are:
CC7 Volume 
CC120 (All sound off)
CC123 (All notes off)

To use vibrato waveforms "to tape" + 1 three times

To use vibrato range "to tape" + 2 three times

To use vibrato targets "to tape" + 3 three times

To use the New Random Mode Arp: press assign button twice

Note: the button presses above are the ones of V2.34. In V2.5 the menus are Imogen's, see "V2.5 includes" below.


IMPORTANT - save your patches before you update -
Before you install a new firmware (V2.5 or any later version), dump all your presets to the computer, and send them back after the update.
The update can erase the presets (the Teensy Loader always does), and V2.5 keeps them in a different place than V2.34.
1) Dump: start recording sysex on the computer (any sysex program, e.g. SysEx Librarian or MIDI-OX), then
   in V2.34 and older: press "from tape" + 6 ("presets dumped" scrolls by),
   in V2.5: press "from tape" + "record" (patch management, the preset LED lights), then "preset" (dumps all presets), then "record" to leave.
   Stop recording and save the file.
2) Install the new firmware (see "Updating from V2.34" below).
3) Restore: press "from tape" + "record" (patch management), send the saved sysex file, wait until it is sent (the display shows the number of each
   patch as it arrives), then press "record" to leave. V2.34 patches are converted to V2.5 automatically.
4) Recall: press "preset", then the two digit number.
Important: patch management must be on while you send. If it is off, the patches are only played, not stored.


V2.5 includes -
V2.5 is built on Imogen's version of the firmware (as used in the Flat-Labs Z80P600 board) instead of GliGli V2.1 RC3. Everything from V2.34 is still there: the 12 LFO waveforms, the noise level control, vibrato waveforms, range and targets, the bender targets PW and VCO B, poly-mod env to VCO A, VCO B or both, channel and poly aftertouch, CC7, CC120, CC123 and the random arp mode.

Changed from V2.34:
Step4 and Step8 now run at the same speed as Saw (they were 4 and 8 times slower), Step4 has 4 steps (it had 2) and Bit_Sine has 16 steps (it had 64).
Poly aftertouch opens the filter of the voice playing that note (up to 3 octaves).
Patches made before V2.25 get a triangle vibrato at normal speed.

New in V2.5:
Arpeggiator: Euclidean rhythms (3-8, 5-8, 7-8, 5-16, 7-16, 9-16, 11-16), step probability, swing, resolution (16ths, 16th triplets, 32nds, 32nd triplets), ratchets (2, 3 or 4 hits per step) and ratchet probability. Off or 100% is the old arp.
Ensemble vibrato: in unison each voice gets its own vibrato phase (small or wide).
Vibrato targets: VCO, VCA, VCO A, VCO B, noise, resonance, detune and poly-mod amount (VCO B).
Poly-mod env targets: VCO A, VCO B, both, PW A, PW B, both PW.
From Imogen's firmware: vintage (voice spread), drive and mix (SCI panel layout), env routing, LFO trigger and sync, assign mode, pot pick-up, local on/off, more pitch modes, polyphonic sequencer, mod wheel range curves.
Faster: the panel and keyboard scan and the S&H updates use less of the CPU, the pitch bender is read twice as often.
Presets and settings are checked when they are loaded, so a damaged patch can not crash the synth.
Boot light show (switch it off with "from tape" + 7) and the welcome text "P600 Matrix edition Ver 2.5".

Pictures: documentation/V2.5 LFO waveforms.pdf (all 12 LFO and vibrato shapes) and documentation/V2.5 arp Euclidean rhythms.pdf (the 8 rhythms).

To use (preset mode: press "to tape" first, then the number; pressing the same number again goes to the next parameter of that number):
"to tape" + 0: speed, Euclid, probability, swing, resolution, ratchet, ratchet probability
"to tape" + 1: LFO shape, LFO target, LFO trigger
"to tape" + 2: vibrato speed, vibrato amount, vibrato target, ensemble, vibrato shape, vibrato range
"to tape" + 3: mod wheel target, mod delay, mod wheel range
"to tape" + 4: pitch mode, noise (shown as "ext volt"), pulse bug
"to tape" + 5: filter env shape, 2nd env shape, env routing, poly-mod env target
"to tape" + 6: bender target, bender range
"to tape" + 7: priority, assign mode, glide
"to tape" + 8: detune, vintage, drive (SCI layout only)
"to tape" + 9: amp velocity, filter velocity

"from tape" + number: 0 local on/off, 1 MIDI in channel, 2 MIDI out channel, 3 bender calibration, 4 and 5 voice select and voice off, 6 panel layout (GliGli or SCI), 7 light show on/off, 8 sync, 9 VCF limit, "preset" basic patch, "seq 1" reset settings (and retune).

To dump all presets: "from tape" + "record" (patch management), then "preset". "record" leaves patch management. (In V2.34 this was "from tape" + 6.)

To use the random arp: press assign button twice (same as V2.34).

MIDI CCs: stepped parameters are CC 48 + parameter number, as before, but the parameter order is Imogen's, so some numbers changed: vibrato shape is now CC115 and vibrato range CC116 (were CC74 and CC75), CC57 LFO shape, CC68 bender target, CC72 vibrato target, CC78 arp Euclid, CC79 arp probability. CC48-50 are mix, glide/vol B and drive. The V2.34 Ctrlr panels need updating for V2.5.


Updating from V2.34 -
V2.5 is about 77 KB, so it does not fit below the 64 KB mark where V2.34 kept the presets. The presets have moved. Settings (your tuning), sequences and the manual patch stay where they were.

To keep your patches: dump them first and restore them after the update, see "IMPORTANT - save your patches before you update" above.

By sysex (p600firmware V2.5.syx): hold "from tape" + "to tape" while switching on, send the file, wait for "S" on the display, switch off and on.
If it shows "E", start again (send slower if it repeats). Settings, tuning, sequences and the manual patch are kept; the presets are empty
(V2.34 presets 96-99 show up as 0-3) until you restore your dump.

With the Teensy Loader (p600firmware V2.5.hex): press the button on the Teensy and load the file. This erases presets, settings and sequences:
restore your dump and press "tune" afterwards. Use this if a sysex update does not start any more.

Fixed in V2.5 (Teensy part):
The startup code could skip setting the initial values of the variables, depending on the compiler version.
The sysex updater no longer calls into the program it is replacing.
Saving to flash goes through the Teensy bootloader; the registers the program needs are now kept across it (a save crashed the synth) and the watchdog is switched off.
The settings are only saved at power on when they had to be made new (as in V2.34).
Keys, buttons and display are scanned as in V2.34 (the Flat-Labs way left the display and LEDs dark on the Teensy).


Thanks -
GliGli: none of this exists without GliGli's firmware. Replacing the Z80 with a Teensy and rewriting the whole P600 firmware brought presets, arpeggiator, sequencer, MIDI, unison, auto tuning and so much more to the Prophet 600. http://gligli.github.io/p600fw/

Imogen: Imogen's version is a massive rework and extension of GliGli's code, with new envelopes and routing, LFO sync, the polyphonic sequencer, vintage spread, the SCI panel layout, pot pick-up, patch management and many fixes. V2.5 is built on it. https://github.com/image-et-son/p600fw

Also thanks to Flat-Labs (Z80P600 board and firmware port), JHHL (new LFO shapes), JAM (arp up/down and random mode) and Overcycler (RevSaw).


